step Expert Leatherworking
  tip Expert raises the cap from 150 to 225; it needs Leatherworking 125 and character level 20, so you can take it on any visit from 125. Only a few trainers teach it: Alliance Telonis (Darnassus); Horde Una (Thunder Bluff). This route trains it at Telonis (Darnassus) for the Alliance and Una (Thunder Bluff) for the Horde, who also teach the recipes of 150-225: one trainer for every visit. Learn now: Barbaric Shoulders (from 150). 150-225 takes about 7g 61s 50c of vendor goods, plus 398 Thick Leather to gather or buy. Come with all of it in your bags (the steps above, the rest from the Auction House): these trainers also teach Guardian Gloves (from 165) and Nightscape Headband (from 180), and the crafts need no station, so craft right here and learn each recipe as you reach its skill. One trip instead of 3. Nightscape Pants (from 205) takes a second trip, to other trainers (below).
  level 20
  train Leatherworking Expert npc 4212 only Alliance
  train Leatherworking Expert npc 3007 only Horde
  learn 7151 npc 4212 only Alliance
  learn 7151 npc 3007 only Horde

step Heavy Armor Kit to 158
  tip Heavy Armor Kit is yellow at 150 (yellow 145, green 155, grey 165): about 15 crafts to 158, up to 20 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 5 Heavy Leather and 1 Fine Thread. Five Heavy Leather a craft (beasts of level 28-40); the kits sell to vendors. If you got here without learning Heavy Armor Kit, learn it now: an earlier step teaches it.
  learn 3780
  craft 3780 until 158

step Barbaric Shoulders to 165
  tip Barbaric Shoulders is orange at 158 (yellow 170, green 180, grey 190): about 7 crafts to 165, a point every craft. Each takes 8 Heavy Leather, 1 Cured Heavy Hide and 2 Fine Thread. Use the 7 Cured Heavy Hide you made earlier; the counts above leave them out. The trainer teaches it, and it is the cheapest way through these points in the data.
  craft 7151 until 165

step Leatherworking recipes at 165
  tip Still at the Expert trainer: Guardian Gloves (from 165).
  learn 7156 npc 4212 only Alliance
  learn 7156 npc 3007 only Horde

step Guardian Gloves to 180
  tip Guardian Gloves is orange at 165 (yellow 185, green 195, grey 205): about 15 crafts to 180, a point every craft. Each takes 4 Heavy Leather, 1 Cured Heavy Hide and 1 Silken Thread. Make the 5 Cured Heavy Hide first. Use the 10 Cured Heavy Hide you made earlier; the counts above leave them out. The trainer teaches it, and it is the cheapest way through these points in the data. If you got here without learning Cured Heavy Hide, learn it now: an earlier step teaches it.
  learn 3818
  craft 3818 x5
  craft 7156 until 180

step Leatherworking recipes at 180
  tip Still at the Expert trainer: Nightscape Headband (from 180).
  learn 10507 npc 4212 only Alliance
  learn 10507 npc 3007 only Horde

step Nightscape Headband to 213
  tip Nightscape Headband is orange at 180 (yellow 200, green 210, grey 220): about 41 crafts to 213, up to 46 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 5 Thick Leather and 2 Silken Thread. The trainer teaches it, and it is the cheapest way through these points in the data.
  craft 10507 until 213

step Leatherworking recipes at 213
  tip Nightscape Pants (from 205) is taught only by the Artisan trainers: Alliance Drakk Stonehand (The Hinterlands); Horde Hahrana Ironhide (Feralas). You can train Artisan there now if you are level 35 (it needs Leatherworking 200), which saves the trip at 225.
  learn 10548 npc 11097 only Alliance map 1425
  learn 10548 npc 11098 only Horde
  train Leatherworking Artisan optional

step Nightscape Pants to 225
  tip Nightscape Pants is orange at 213 (yellow 225, green 235, grey 245): about 12 crafts to 225, a point every craft. Each takes 14 Thick Leather and 4 Silken Thread. The trainer teaches it, and it is the cheapest way through these points in the data. Leatherworking 225 is a Legacy System milestone.
  craft 10548 until 225
  skill Leatherworking 225

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Artisan (225-300)
section Leatherworking 225-300

step Artisan Leatherworking
  tip Artisan raises the cap from 225 to 300; it needs Leatherworking 200 and character level 35, so you can take it on any visit from 200. Only a few trainers teach it: Alliance Drakk Stonehand (The Hinterlands); Horde Hahrana Ironhide (Feralas). This route trains it at Drakk Stonehand (The Hinterlands) for the Alliance and Hahrana Ironhide (Feralas) for the Horde, who also teach the recipes of 225-300: one trainer for every visit. Learn now: Rugged Armor Kit (from 225). 225-300 takes about 3g 40s of recipes and 44g 90s of vendor goods, plus 1205 Rugged Leather and 500 Runecloth to gather or buy.
  level 35
  train Leatherworking Artisan npc 11097 only Alliance map 1425
  train Leatherworking Artisan npc 11098 only Horde
  learn 19058 npc 11097 only Alliance map 1425
  learn 19058 npc 11098 only Horde

step Leatherworking 225-300: vendor goods
  tip Buy the whole bracket's share in one go: 39 Black Dye (3g 90s) and 82 Rune Thread (41g); about 44g 90s in all. The arrow picks the nearest seller of your faction (Stormwind City: Alexandra Bolero and Jillian Tanner; Orgrimmar: Borya and Tamar).
  buy 2325 x39 nearest
  buy 14341 x82 nearest

step Pattern: Wicked Leather Gauntlets
  tip Pattern: Wicked Leather Gauntlets teaches Wicked Leather Gauntlets (Leatherworking 235) for 1g 20s. Sold by Alliance: Leonard Porter (Western Plaguelands), limited stock; Horde: Werg Thickblade (Western Plaguelands), limited stock. Its sellers keep one or two in stock that come back some time after a sale; it binds when picked up, so the Auction House never has it.
  buy 15725 nearest

step Pattern: Runic Leather Headband
  tip Pattern: Runic Leather Headband teaches Runic Leather Headband (Leatherworking 265) for 2g 20s. Sold by Jase Farlane (Eastern Plaguelands), limited stock. Its sellers keep one or two in stock that come back some time after a sale; it binds when picked up, so the Auction House never has it.
  buy 15756 nearest

step Get Rugged Leather
  tip 1205 Rugged Leather for Leatherworking 225-300: 29 Rugged Armor Kits, 45 Wicked Leather Gauntlets and 50 Runic Leather Headbands. Skinning: beasts of level 48-60. The window lists the Skinning areas for your level, best first: the arrow leads to the one you pick and rests there until your bags hold them. Or buy them at the Auction House.
  collect 8170 x1205 gather Skinning 225
